{
  "nodes": [
    {
      "id": "a34f7cccfdb34c53",
      "type": "text",
      "text": "# ☸️ Master Architecture\n## Buddhist Teachings & Principles\n\nCentral interactive hub connecting canonical scriptures, core doctrines, people, geography, stories, and living somatic application.\n\n[[_Master Mind Map - Buddhist Teachings and Principles|Open Master Hub Note]]",
      "x": -250,
      "y": -120,
      "width": 500,
      "height": 240,
      "color": "6"
    },
    {
      "id": "f007b0a71c434ba6",
      "type": "group",
      "label": "BRANCH 1: CORE BUDDHIST PRINCIPLES (9 PILLARS)",
      "x": -1320,
      "y": -1150,
      "width": 2520,
      "height": 980,
      "color": "6"
    },
    {
      "id": "1096346f3a1d49c0",
      "type": "text",
      "text": "### ☸️ Core Buddhist Principles\n**The 9 Foundational Pillars**\n[[_Master Mind Map - Core Buddhist Principles|Open Core Principles Note]]",
      "x": -200,
      "y": -1100,
      "width": 400,
      "height": 120,
      "color": "6"
    },
    {
      "id": "c291d1aa415143d1",
      "type": "text",
      "text": "#### 1. The 3 Universal Truths\nTilakkha\\u1e47a:\\n- Anicca (Impermanence)\\n- Dukkha (Unsatisfactoriness)\\n- Anatt\\u0101 (Not-Self / Non-Owner)",
      "x": -1050,
      "y": -920,
      "width": 320,
      "height": 200,
      "color": "6"
    },
    {
      "id": "2af4e2abba9b417d",
      "type": "text",
      "text": "#### [[Report - The Four Noble Truths - Cattāri Ariyasaccāni and the Four Noble Duties|2. The Four Noble Truths]]\nCattāri Ariyasaccāni & 4 Tasks:\n- Dukkha (To be understood)\n- Samudaya / Craving (Abandoned)\n- Nirodha / Cessation (Realized)\n- Magga / Path (Cultivated)\n\n[[Report - The Four Noble Truths - Cattāri Ariyasaccāni and the Four Noble Duties|Open Study Report: 4 Noble Truths & 4 Duties ↗]]",
      "x": -700,
      "y": -920,
      "width": 320,
      "height": 240,
      "color": "6"
    },
    {
      "id": "a5eee51f8d45487f",
      "type": "text",
      "text": "#### 3. The Eightfold Path\nAriyo A\\u1e6d\\u1e6dha\\u1e45giko Maggo:\\n- Pa\\u00f1\\u00f1\\u0101 (Right View, Resolve)\\n- S\\u012bla (Action, Speech, Livelihood)\\n- Sam\\u0101dhi (Effort, Mindfulness, Stillness)",
      "x": -350,
      "y": -920,
      "width": 320,
      "height": 200,
      "color": "6"
    },
    {
      "id": "e17ce0a1440e4e73",
      "type": "text",
      "text": "#### 4. Precepts & Vinaya\nS\\u012bla & Avippa\\u1e6dis\\u0101ra:\\n- Pa\\u00f1cas\\u012bla (5 Lay Precepts)\\n- A\\u1e6d\\u1e6dha\\u1e45gas\\u012bla (8 Uposatha)\\n- Freedom from remorse & clear conscience",
      "x": 0,
      "y": -920,
      "width": 320,
      "height": 200,
      "color": "6"
    },
    {
      "id": "cb4437a9002b4e7d",
      "type": "text",
      "text": "#### 5. The 3 Poisons\nAkusalam\\u016bla (Unwholesome Roots):\\n- Lobha (Greed / Grasping)\\n- Dosa (Aversion / Irritation)\\n- Moha (Delusion / Unknowing)",
      "x": 350,
      "y": -920,
      "width": 320,
      "height": 200,
      "color": "6"
    },
    {
      "id": "902d862892f84335",
      "type": "text",
      "text": "#### 6. Karma & Volition\nKamma & Cetan\\u0101:\\n- Intention is the deed\\n- Vip\\u0101ka (Fruit / Result)\\n- Conditionality (Idappaccayat\\u0101)",
      "x": 700,
      "y": -920,
      "width": 320,
      "height": 200,
      "color": "6"
    },
    {
      "id": "ab54411222a8461e",
      "type": "text",
      "text": "#### [[Concentration_In_Buddhist_Lists|7. Meditation & Stillness]]\nBhāvanā:\n- Samatha (Tranquility / Calm)\n- Vipassanā (Insight / Clear Seeing)\n- 4 Rūpa Jhānas & Somatic Presence\n\n[[Concentration_In_Buddhist_Lists|Open Study Report: Concentration Across Buddhist Lists ↗]]",
      "x": -210,
      "y": -670,
      "width": 320,
      "height": 240,
      "color": "6"
    },
    {
      "id": "fd003357a4b746da",
      "type": "text",
      "text": "#### 8. The Brahmavih\\u0101ras\nThe 4 Immeasurables:\\n- Mett\\u0101 (Goodwill / Friendliness)\\n- Karu\\u1e47\\u0101 (Compassion for suffering)\\n- Mudit\\u0101 (Sympathetic Joy)\\n- Upekkh\\u0101 (Grounded Equanimity)",
      "x": -175,
      "y": -560,
      "width": 320,
      "height": 200,
      "color": "6"
    },
    {
      "id": "3edaad55ede2437f",
      "type": "text",
      "text": "#### 9. The 10 Fetters\nDasa Sa\\u1e43yojan\\u0101ni:\\n- Lower 5: Identity view, doubt, rites, sensual desire, ill will\\n- Higher 5: Subtle conceit, restlessness, ignorance",
      "x": 490,
      "y": -670,
      "width": 320,
      "height": 220,
      "color": "6"
    },
    {
      "id": "f558dfb093f649c7",
      "type": "group",
      "label": "BRANCH 2: THE TIPIṬAKA (CANONICAL COLLECTION)",
      "x": 1200,
      "y": -1150,
      "width": 1250,
      "height": 950,
      "color": "5"
    },
    {
      "id": "20605a4867b645e0",
      "type": "text",
      "text": "### 📜 The Tipiṭaka\n**The Three Baskets of Canonical Wisdom**\n[[_Master Mind Map - The Tipitaka|Open Tipiṭaka Note]]",
      "x": 1650,
      "y": -1100,
      "width": 380,
      "height": 120,
      "color": "5"
    },
    {
      "id": "234a7fae4d524eaa",
      "type": "text",
      "text": "#### Sutta Piṭaka (Discourses)\n- **Dīgha Nikāya**: Long Discourses (34 suttas)\\n- **Majjhima Nikāya**: Middle-Length (152 suttas)\\n- **Saṃyutta Nikāya**: Connected (2,889 suttas)\\n- **Aṅguttara Nikāya**: Numerical (8,700+ suttas)\\n- **Khuddaka Nikāya**: Minor (Dhammapada, Jātaka, Apadāna, Theragāthā, Therīgāthā)",
      "x": 1250,
      "y": -920,
      "width": 360,
      "height": 420,
      "color": "5"
    },
    {
      "id": "ace0b1b6a17a4bf3",
      "type": "text",
      "text": "#### Vinaya Piṭaka (Monastic Discipline)\n- **Suttavibhaṅga**: Pātimokkha rules for Bhikkhus (227) & Bhikkhunīs (311)\\n- **Khandhaka**: Mahāvagga & Cullavagga (Ordination, community life, disputes)\\n- **Parivāra**: Analytical summaries & training manuals",
      "x": 1650,
      "y": -920,
      "width": 360,
      "height": 300,
      "color": "5"
    },
    {
      "id": "4b1c27bb657d4f40",
      "type": "text",
      "text": "#### Abhidhamma Piṭaka (Higher Doctrine)\n- **Dhammasaṅgaṇī**: Enumeration of ultimate phenomena\\n- **Vibhaṅga**: Analysis of aggregates, sense bases, truths\\n- **Dhātukathā & Puggalapaññatti**: Elements & personality types\\n- **Kathāvatthu, Yamaka & Paṭṭhāna**: Dialectics, pairs & 24 conditional relations",
      "x": 2050,
      "y": -920,
      "width": 360,
      "height": 350,
      "color": "5"
    },
    {
      "id": "b2d107e665fd4657",
      "type": "group",
      "label": "BRANCH 3: DRAMATIS PERSONAE (PEOPLE & INTERLOCUTORS)",
      "x": 1200,
      "y": -100,
      "width": 1250,
      "height": 920,
      "color": "4"
    },
    {
      "id": "09e9d58f058248b9",
      "type": "text",
      "text": "### 👥 Dramatis Personae\n**Interlocutors, Monastics & Benefactors**\n[[_Master Mind Map - Dramatis Personae|Open Dramatis Personae Note]]",
      "x": 1650,
      "y": -50,
      "width": 380,
      "height": 120,
      "color": "4"
    },
    {
      "id": "079b656a7f234d80",
      "type": "text",
      "text": "#### Senior Monastics & Chiefs\n- **Sāriputta**: Chief in Wisdom & analysis\\n- **Mahāmoggallāna**: Chief in Psychic powers & exertion\\n- **Ānanda**: Chief in Hearing, Attendant & Memory\\n- **Mahākassapa**: Chief in Austere practices (dhutaṅga)\\n- **Anuruddha**: Chief in Divine eye & mindfulness",
      "x": 1250,
      "y": 120,
      "width": 360,
      "height": 280,
      "color": "4"
    },
    {
      "id": "9944304cabb1426f",
      "type": "text",
      "text": "#### Lay Disciples & Benefactors\n- **Anāthapiṇḍika**: Feeder of the poor, purchaser of Jetavana\\n- **Visākhā Migāramātā**: Chief benefactress of the Sangha\\n- **Jīvaka Komārabhacca**: Royal physician, medicine & ethics\\n- **Citta the Householder**: Master of Dhamma discourse",
      "x": 1650,
      "y": 120,
      "width": 360,
      "height": 260,
      "color": "4"
    },
    {
      "id": "7fdcbc558c7741e2",
      "type": "text",
      "text": "#### Royal Interlocutors\n- **King Pasenadi of Kosala**: Intimate conversations on aging & statecraft\\n- **King Bimbisāra of Magadha**: Early royal patron\\n- **King Ajātasattu**: Parricide, remorse & Sāmaññaphala Sutta",
      "x": 2050,
      "y": 120,
      "width": 360,
      "height": 240,
      "color": "4"
    },
    {
      "id": "4e904beb379b4eb7",
      "type": "text",
      "text": "#### Wanderers & Seekers\n- **Vacchagotta**: Questions on self, the cosmos, and fire extinguishing\\n- **Dīghanakha**: Extreme philosophical views dismantled\\n- **Potthapāda**: Nature of perception and cessation\\n- **Bāhiya Dārucīriya**: Instant awakening: In the seen, only the seen",
      "x": 1250,
      "y": 440,
      "width": 360,
      "height": 280,
      "color": "4"
    },
    {
      "id": "e2270e85724b4e92",
      "type": "text",
      "text": "#### Transformative Figures\n- **Aṅgulimāla**: Bandit turned Arahant; stopping in Dhamma\\n- **Paṭācārā & Kisa Gotamī**: Overwhelming grief transformed into liberating wisdom\\n- **Sunīta the Outcaste**: Road-sweeper elevated by universal Dhamma",
      "x": 1650,
      "y": 440,
      "width": 360,
      "height": 280,
      "color": "4"
    },
    {
      "id": "279d9ba1a0e94c80",
      "type": "group",
      "label": "BRANCH 4: CANONICAL LOCATIONS (NIDĀNA / GEOGRAPHY)",
      "x": 1200,
      "y": 900,
      "width": 1250,
      "height": 650,
      "color": "2"
    },
    {
      "id": "632deae501274c8a",
      "type": "text",
      "text": "### 🏛️ Canonical Locations\n**Nidāna: Physical Settings & Sacred Geography**\n[[_Master Mind Map - Canonical Locations|Open Locations Note]]",
      "x": 1650,
      "y": 950,
      "width": 380,
      "height": 120,
      "color": "2"
    },
    {
      "id": "7eb19bd76c06417b",
      "type": "text",
      "text": "#### Sāvatthī (Kosala)\n- **Jetavana**: Anāthapiṇḍika’s grove (majority of MN/SN)\\n- **Pubbārāma**: Migāramātā’s mansion\\n- **Andhavana**: Blind Man’s Grove (solitary meditation)",
      "x": 1250,
      "y": 1120,
      "width": 360,
      "height": 220,
      "color": "2"
    },
    {
      "id": "5ff658d429684e5c",
      "type": "text",
      "text": "#### Rājagaha (Magadha)\n- **Gijjhakūṭa**: Vulture Peak\\n- **Veḷuvana**: Bamboo Grove (King Bimbisāra)\\n- **Jīvaka’s Mango Grove**: Medical refuge & serene healing",
      "x": 1650,
      "y": 1120,
      "width": 360,
      "height": 220,
      "color": "2"
    },
    {
      "id": "dff1b8cbaa01473d",
      "type": "text",
      "text": "#### Vesālī, Kosambi & Kapilavatthu\n- **Vesālī**: Mahāvana & Kūṭāgārasālā (Gabled Hall)\\n- **Kosambi**: Ghositārāma (monastic reconciliation)\\n- **Kapilavatthu**: Nigrodhārāma (hometown return)",
      "x": 2050,
      "y": 1120,
      "width": 360,
      "height": 220,
      "color": "2"
    },
    {
      "id": "2efabc9570f240ff",
      "type": "group",
      "label": "BRANCH 5: STORIES, PARABLES & BIOGRAPHIES",
      "x": -1100,
      "y": 900,
      "width": 2200,
      "height": 650,
      "color": "1"
    },
    {
      "id": "baad715f80b4440b",
      "type": "text",
      "text": "### 📖 Stories, Parables & Biographies\n**Apadāna Saints, Jātakas & Canonical Similes**\n[[_Master Mind Map - Stories and Parables|Open Stories Note]] • [[Buddhist Biographies|Biographies ↗]]",
      "x": -200,
      "y": 950,
      "width": 430,
      "height": 130,
      "color": "1"
    },
    {
      "id": "7de17573abcf4321",
      "type": "text",
      "text": "#### The Apadāna (Legends of Saints)\nJonathan Walters Translation (1,197 pp):\n- 550+ Bhikkhu Apadānas (past merit to final Arahantship)\n- 40+ Bhikkhunī Apadānas (heroism, patience & liberation)\n- Karmic link between aeons of practice and immediate fruit\n\n<small>[[Buddhist Biographies|Detailed Profiles: 32 Early Saints & Benefactors ↗]]</small>",
      "x": -1050,
      "y": 1120,
      "width": 680,
      "height": 260,
      "color": "1"
    },
    {
      "id": "11d97743c1274c98",
      "type": "text",
      "text": "#### The Jātakas (Bodhisatta Path)\n547 Birth Tales:\\n- Cultivation of the 10 Pāramīs across lifetimes\\n- Animal allegories, royal self-sacrifice & moral dilemmas\\n- Foundational narrative bedrock of Buddhist compassion",
      "x": -320,
      "y": 1120,
      "width": 680,
      "height": 240,
      "color": "1"
    },
    {
      "id": "6e410fae3fb040b4",
      "type": "text",
      "text": "#### Master Similes of the Suttas\nTransformative Metaphors:\\n- **The Raft**: For crossing, not for clinging\\n- **The Two Darts (Sallatha Sutta)**: Physical sensation vs reactive dukkha\\n- **The Blind Turtle**: The unfathomable rarity of human birth\\n- **The Mountain**: Aging & death rolling in from the 4 quarters\n- **Living Forest Similes (Ajahn Chah)**: The Broken Glass, Disturbing the Car, Bailing the Drum ([[#4 Living Forest Tradition Parables & Similes of Luang Por Chah|_Ajahn Chah stories_ ↗]])",
      "x": 410,
      "y": 1120,
      "width": 650,
      "height": 280,
      "color": "1"
    },
    {
      "id": "a41b973075274538",
      "type": "group",
      "label": "BRANCH 6: PĀLI LEXICON & DOCTRINAL INDEX",
      "x": -2400,
      "y": -400,
      "width": 1200,
      "height": 650,
      "color": "3"
    },
    {
      "id": "422b5e3a761b4956",
      "type": "text",
      "text": "### 📚 Pāli Lexicon & Doctrinal Index\n**Root Meanings, Etymology & Precise Vocabulary**\n[[_Master Mind Map - Pali Lexicon|Open Pāli Lexicon Note]]\n[[Pali to English Dictionary|Open Master Dictionary]]",
      "x": -1950,
      "y": -350,
      "width": 380,
      "height": 150,
      "color": "3"
    },
    {
      "id": "cac566c3b3cd47d4",
      "type": "text",
      "text": "#### Master Pāli Dictionary Integration\n- Direct synchronization with master vault dictionary\\n- Systematic 7-field schema (Root, Category, Doctrinal Definition, Sutta Citations)\\n- Technical monastic & philosophical terms",
      "x": -2350,
      "y": -160,
      "width": 360,
      "height": 250,
      "color": "3"
    },
    {
      "id": "337e0bcb7edf4759",
      "type": "text",
      "text": "#### Key Canonical Concepts\n- **Indriyasamvara**: Guarding the sense doors\\n- **Upāyakosalla**: Skill in means / tailored teaching\\n- **Yoniso Manasikāra**: Appropriate attention\\n- **Papañca**: Mental proliferation & storytelling",
      "x": -1950,
      "y": -160,
      "width": 360,
      "height": 250,
      "color": "3"
    },
    {
      "id": "09b0f6fe21fe4e9f",
      "type": "text",
      "text": "#### Conditionality & Dependent Origination\n- **Idappaccayatā**: Specific conditionality (*When this is, that is*)\\n- **Paṭiccasamuppāda**: 12 links of dependent origination\\n- **Kilesa & Āsava**: Defilements & deep taints",
      "x": -1550,
      "y": -160,
      "width": 360,
      "height": 250,
      "color": "3"
    },
    {
      "id": "a4aa1c8f94754a15",
      "type": "group",
      "label": "BRANCH 7: LIVING LINEAGES & PRACTICAL APPLICATION",
      "x": -2680,
      "y": 360,
      "width": 1540,
      "height": 510,
      "color": "5"
    },
    {
      "id": "e1b06077471b4412",
      "type": "text",
      "text": "### 🌿 Living Lineages & Practical Application\n**Forest Tradition, Somatics & Mindful Living**\n[[_Master Mind Map - Living Lineages and Practice|Open Lineages Note]]",
      "x": -2095,
      "y": 400,
      "width": 380,
      "height": 130,
      "color": "5"
    },
    {
      "id": "7b65f427965e4ba9",
      "type": "text",
      "text": "#### 🌲 Thai Forest Tradition\n- **Root**: Ajahn Mun Bhūridatto (Wilderness *Kammaṭṭhāna*)\n- **Wat Nong Pah Pong**: Luang Por Chah Subhaddo\n  - *Master Retrospective & Archives*: [[Report - Ajahn Chah - Historic Teachings at Insight Meditation Society (June 16, 1979)|IMS 1979 Master Report ↗]] • [[_Ajahn Chah stories_|28 Master Stories & Parables ↗]]\n  - *Full Canon*: 60 Complete Dharma Talk Reports (IMS 1979 Sessions + All 56 Chapters of *The Collected Teachings*)\n- **Non-Thai Elders** (descended from Mun via Chah):\n  - *Ajahn Sumedho* (*Nāda* silence, *Buddho*, Mother's heart)\n  - *Ajahn Pasanno* (Friend to the breath, steadfast poise)\n  - *Ajahn Amaro* (Unentangled awareness, non-duality)\n  - *Ajahn Sucitto* (Somatic knot, embodied interoception)\n  - *Ajahn Nyaniko* (Looking into dukkha, Abhayagiri abbot)\n- **Dhammayut Lineage & Master Sutta Translator**:\n  - *Thanissaro Bhikkhu* (Ajaan Fuang / Ajaan Lee lineage; master translator of Nikāyas & breath energy)\n\n<small>[[Report - The Thai Forest Tradition - Roots, Lineage Architecture, and Living Masters|Detailed Lineage Study Report ↗]]</small>",
      "x": -2630,
      "y": 570,
      "width": 350,
      "height": 450,
      "color": "5"
    },
    {
      "id": "332bcb68f3d14d21",
      "type": "text",
      "text": "#### Somatic Mindfulness & Threat Biology\n- Somatic contractions (belly tight/knotted) as biological survival reactions\\n- **Deer vs Human**: Deer shakes off fear; *we think about the tiger when there is no tiger*\\n- Polyvagal safety, sensing into the physical body",
      "x": -2260,
      "y": 570,
      "width": 330,
      "height": 260,
      "color": "5"
    },
    {
      "id": "e73e3221b11f4fd8",
      "type": "text",
      "text": "#### Everyday Living & Recovery\n- **Rewiring Stress Habit**: Converting chronic reactivity into grounded peace\\n- Everyday realities: Checkout counters, utility bills, sensory contacts\\n- Freedom from remorse (*avippaṭisāra*) as practical daily refuge",
      "x": -1890,
      "y": 570,
      "width": 330,
      "height": 260,
      "color": "5"
    },
    {
      "id": "44b63bdcfa254ea3",
      "type": "text",
      "x": -1240,
      "y": -670,
      "width": 240,
      "height": 85,
      "color": "6",
      "text": "**[[Universal_Truth_1_Anicca_Impermanence_and_the_Flow_of_Experience|Anicca]]**\nImpermanence"
    },
    {
      "id": "05dee75b17ac4608",
      "type": "text",
      "x": -930,
      "y": -670,
      "width": 240,
      "height": 85,
      "color": "6",
      "text": "**[[Universal_Truth_2_Dukkha_The_Architecture_of_Stress_and_Unsatisfactoriness|Dukkha]]**\nUnsatisfactoriness"
    },
    {
      "id": "e6c59a841a624b7a",
      "type": "text",
      "x": -620,
      "y": -670,
      "width": 240,
      "height": 85,
      "color": "6",
      "text": "**[[Universal_Truth_3_Anatta_Non_Self_and_the_Release_of_Ownership|Anattā]]**\nNot-Self"
    },
    {
      "id": "b6f84c107e334a19",
      "type": "text",
      "text": "#### 👥 Sangha & Spiritual Community\n- **The Whole of the Holy Life**: *Kalyāṇamittatā* (*SN 45.2 Upaddha Sutta*)\n- **The Rock Tumbler**: Polishing conceit & sharp edges in community\n- **Living in Concord**: Blending like milk & water (*MN 31 & MN 48*)\n\n<small>[[Report - The Importance of Sangha - Community, Spiritual Friendship, and the Living Refuge|Detailed Study Note ↗]]</small>",
      "x": -1520,
      "y": 570,
      "width": 330,
      "height": 260,
      "color": "5"
    },
    {
      "id": "western_insight_neuro_b7",
      "type": "text",
      "text": "#### 🌸 Western Insight, Mindfulness Therapies & Applied Science\n**Bridging Classical Satipaṭṭhāna, Clinical Protocols & Modern Neuroscience**\n\n| Domain | Key Frameworks & Pioneers | Primary Focus & Contemporary Contribution |\n| :--- | :--- | :--- |\n| **Western Insight (Lay Dhamma & Presence)** | **Jack Kornfield**, **Tara Brach**, **Gil Fronsdal**, **James Baraz**, **Eckhart Tolle** | Vipassanā adapted for householders; RAIN emotional compassion; *Awakening Joy*; unconditioned presence (*The Power of Now*); domestic practice. |\n| **Mindfulness-Based Therapies (Clinical)** | **MBSR** *(Kabat-Zinn)*, **MBCT** *(Segal/Williams)*, **ACT** *(Hayes)*, **MBRP** *(Marlatt/Bowen)*, **DBT** *(Linehan)* | Hospital and clinical protocols: de-centering from depressive loops; cognitive defusion (*dropping papañca*); urge surfing at *vedanā*; distress tolerance. |\n| **Medical, Trauma & Neuroscience** | **Dr. John Sarno** *(TMS)*, **Dr. Gabor Maté** *(Trauma/Addiction)*, **Dr. Joe Dispenza**, **Polyvagal Theory** *(Porges)* | Psychosomatic pain as emotional diversion; trauma physiology (*When the Body Says No*); biological neuroplasticity; ventral vagal mammalian safety. |\n\n<small>[[_Master Mind Map - Living Lineages and Practice#5 Western Insight Mindfulness Therapies and Applied Modern Sciences|Detailed Lineages, Clinical Therapies & Research Hub ↗]]</small>",
      "x": -2270,
      "y": 1735,
      "width": 1100,
      "height": 340
    }
  ],
  "edges": [
    {
